From: Dallas Delaney <dadelan@microsoft.com>
Subject: [PATCH] erofs: ACL dm-verity integration, off by default

Squash of two commits on the ACL containerd branch, applied on top of
Patch8:

  erofs: derive dm-verity referrer discovery from the differ
  erofs: support dm-verity referrers on OCI-layout imports

Patch8 wires the dm-verity referrer handler unconditionally into every
pull and every CRI image pull, so every existing EROFS user pays a
referrers round trip on upgrade whether or not anything on the node
consumes the result. This derives discovery from the differ that consumes
what it finds rather than adding a setting for it: the erofs differ
advertises a dmverity-referrers capability when enable_dmverity is set,
which the transfer service and the CRI image service each read. With no
configuration present, stock upstream EROFS behavior is restored exactly.

On top of that it adds the ACL integration: a content-store fetcher so
OCI-layout imports can satisfy require_signatures (previously the only
entry point that could not), signature writing on the differ's Apply path
whenever a layer carries one, and a move of the layer-blob formatting body
into internal/dmverity as FormatLayerBlob -- next to Format, Open and
ReadMetadata -- with rollback, so a failed format cannot leave a truncated
blob and a partial sidecar behind. A !linux stub keeps the package's
exported surface identical on every platform.

Nothing here touches plugins/snapshots/erofs. Formatting the layer.erofs
that the snapshotter's commitBlock path builds from an overlay upperdir
was considered and rejected: commitBlock has no signature to write, so the
result is unsigned dm-verity, which is integrity without authenticity and
is not enforceable; and nothing breaks without it, because dmverity_mode
defaults to "auto", under which a layer with no sidecar mounts as plain
EROFS.

Doing it is in fact not possible as written. Deciding whether to format
requires knowing whether a differ handles dm-verity, and a snapshotter
cannot learn that at init: the metadata plugin already requires
SnapshotPlugin, so any Requires edge from the erofs snapshotter to
DiffPlugin closes the cycle

    SnapshotPlugin -> DiffPlugin -> MetadataPlugin -> SnapshotPlugin

which Registry.Graph does not detect -- it marks a registration as added
only after recursing into its requirements -- and containerd dies at
startup with a stack overflow. Without the edge the erofs differ
initializes after the erofs snapshotter, so the capability is never
visible and the check silently reads false.

Leaving the snapshotter alone also keeps Patch8's dmverity_mode default of
"auto" untouched, so this patch carries no conflict with Patch8 when the
latter is dropped in favour of an upstream release.

Security corrections folded in (review of the ACL series):
  - Compose the CRI image-handler wrappers instead of overwriting them.
    RemoteContext.HandlerWrapper is a single field, so passing
    WithImageHandlerWrapper twice kept only the last one: enabling dm-verity
    referrers silently dropped the remote-snapshot annotations that
    AppendInfoHandlerWrapper installs for stargz/nydus/overlaybd. Only
    reachable with disable_snapshot_annotations = false, which is not the
    default, but it silently disables an unrelated feature.
  - Generalise the maxManifestSize bound so the same ceiling can guard
    descriptor reads on the registry path in Patch10.

